             'any particular time, or that it is clear now.'),
            ("How long ago a reading's poll was can be bounded only by the runtime that signed "
             "the liveness message the reading's `liveness_nonce` names, only from above, and "
             'only as [How Old A Reading Is](#how-old-a-reading-is) states.'),
            ('Every other receiver cannot bound it.'),
            ("A device delivers buffered readings long after their polls, and the device's uptime "
             "and the receiver's clock run at rates this version does not relate, so a receiver "
             'never infers from accepting a reading recently, or from its `device_uptime_ms`, '
             'that the poll was recent.'),
            ("The signing runtime may present an alarm's state from a reading with a bound as a "
             "snapshot polled no more than A ago, as of T, where A is the reading's bound when it "
