             'reading, any fault hold and the silence bound continue under the active anchor, and '
             'a reading signed under the pending anchor is refused.'),
            ("A message v1's freshness rules refuse, including a duplicate of one already "
             'accepted, is not accepted and changes nothing here.'),
            ('Every alarm on the channel is unknown while the channel has no latest reading, and '
             'while the receiver has accepted no reading for the channel within `3 × '
             'poll_interval_ms + 30000` milliseconds on a monotonic clock that keeps counting '
             "while the receiver's host is suspended: three missed polls and a transport "
             'allowance, which the profile grammar holds to an hour at most.'),
            ('A receiver MAY use a shorter bound and MUST NOT use a longer one.'),
            ('A receiver that restarts has accepted nothing, so every alarm is unknown until it '
             'accepts a reading after the restart.'),
            ('Any accepted reading of the channel restarts the bound, whether or not its age is '
             'bounded.'),
            ('When the receiver accepts a `sensor_fault` naming the channel, every alarm on the '
             'channel is unknown until it accepts a later reading for the channel, or until the '
             'active anchor changes, which leaves no latest reading anyway.'),
            ('This orders the fault and the reading by when each was signed and locates nothing: '
             'under [Late Faults](#late-faults) a fault signed after a recovered reading reports '
